<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">South Korea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Republic of Korea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> (the Republic of Korea) is a state in the southern part of the Korean peninsula, established in 1948. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a> of 1950–1953 it grew under authoritarian governments, above all that of Park Chung-hee, into one of the world's leading industrial economies, and it became a democracy in 1987. Its export-led development was a model for other Asian countries, including Malaysia under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/look-east-policy">Look East Policy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-korea.jpg" alt="South Korea" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Government of the Republic of Korea Vector: Great Brightstar and others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Korea.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
